# S1's "her own equipoise" and S2's "being in equipoise" both mean the earth's balance of its own weight.
# S1's "equability of the surrounding heaven" is reworded as "equably diffused" in P3 and P4; the wording differs but not what would make it true.
# A1 joins two different claims, not inclining and needing no support, each in its own sense, so it is not a bridge.
